    }","fix_hint":"add post(_url: string, _body?: object): Observable&lt;WebReaction&gt; to MockRestService","why_it_matters":"Test-only breakage that could block CI in the follow-up wave.","silenced_marker_nearby":false}],"agent_notes":["Signature change is additive: post(url) became post(url, body?) with an optional parameter, and `body ?? null` keeps the exact old wire behavior for callers that pass no body. This is source- and runtime-compatible.","Existing post() callers I read: model-file.service.ts:61, 74 and 87 (queue/stop/extract/etc.) and server-command.service.ts:26 (restart). None of them pass a body, so they still send a null body with no JSON Content-Type. No behavior change.","When a body object is passed, Angular HttpClient serializes it as JSON and sets Content-Type: application/json automatically. That matches a backend that reads bottle.request.json, which only parses when the Content-Type is application/json.","Edge case: `body ?? null` passes falsy-but-defined values through unchanged. The `object` type already excludes primitives, so this has no practical effect.","Typing `object` is loose: it accepts arrays, Map and so on, and a Map would serialize to {}. Callers are internal, so the risk is low.","Cross-wave risk, outside this diff: in HEAD the backend config/set route is already POST+JSON, but ConfigService.set still issues a GET to the path-param URL (config.service.ts:66-68). Settings saves are therefore broken in the current tree until the frontend wave lands, so do not deploy between waves.","There are no schema or migration changes in this diff and no performance impact. The direct blast radius is limited to the 4 existing post() call sites, all unaffected.","Verdict: the diff is safe and shippable as-is. The only blocking concern is sequencing, meaning the ConfigService migration must land with it before any deploy."]}
